{"title":"1967 AHSME Problems/Problem 9","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1967_AHSME_Problems/Problem_9&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/f/b/dfb064112b6c94470339f6571f69d07afc1c024c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$K$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"19\" height=\"14\" />, in square units, be the area of a trapezoid such that the shorter base, the altitude, and the longer base, in that order, are in arithmetic progression.  Then:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/3/7/8370dd189faea7958ade749dd36947272abb901d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(A)}\\ K \\; \\text{must be an integer} \\qquad \\textbf{(B)}\\ K \\; \\text{must be a rational fraction} \\\\ \\textbf{(C)}\\ K \\; \\text{must be an irrational number} \\qquad \\textbf{(D)}\\ K \\;  \\text{must be an integer or a rational fraction} \\qquad$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"654\" height=\"37\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/8/5/d85edcb5aa156ac429526c37634a4b195cfcee3c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(E)}\\ \\text{taken alone neither} \\; \\textbf{(A)} \\; \\text{nor} \\; \\textbf{(B)} \\; \\text{nor} \\; \\textbf{(C)} \\; \\text{nor} \\; \\textbf{(D)} \\; \\text{is true}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"446\" height=\"17\" />\n</p><p><br />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution\">Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1967_AHSME_Problems/Problem_9&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>From the problem we can set the altitude equal to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/d/c7d457e388298246adb06c587bccd419ea67f7e8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" />, the shorter base equal to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/3/0/730a04d09740e0b0f50d1140c614f6e7840e9bbc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a-d$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"43\" height=\"16\" />, and the longer base equal to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/8/3/b83c9c3a8da8388f2c9107e68f8fe59683cd0cdc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a+d$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"41\" height=\"14\" />. By the formula for the area of a trapezoid, we have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/e/5/de5a651f01d96609752df1ace80dbffd4fbb3ed0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$K=a^2$\" width=\"56\" height=\"15\" />. However, since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/d/c7d457e388298246adb06c587bccd419ea67f7e8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" /> can equal any real number <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/f/a/cfa0805dfa248a472f05f0bb6f3f5832d2757d39.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(3, 2.7, \\pi)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"72\" height=\"18\" />, none of the statements <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/a/7/0a70ef3ff6592247a7bb65ba8bb54d724b112890.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A, B, C, D$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"83\" height=\"18\" /> need to be true, so the answer is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/2/e/62effaf0d5dc9bfa1d137bed40c4baa73698962d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\fbox{E}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"23\" height=\"23\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_also\">See also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1967_AHSME_Problems/Problem_9&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: See also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1967_AHSME\" title=\"1967 AHSME\">1967 AHSC</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1967_AHSME_Problems\" title=\"1967 AHSME Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1967_AHSME_Answer_Key\" title=\"1967 AHSME Answer Key\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"http://www.artofproblemsolving.com/Forum/resources.php?c=182&amp;cid=44&amp;year=1967\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1967_AHSME_Problems/Problem_8\" title=\"1967 AHSME Problems/Problem 8\">Problem 8</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1967_AHSME_Problems/Problem_10\" title=\"1967 AHSME Problems/Problem 10\">Problem 10</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1967_AHSME_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"1967 AHSME Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1967_AHSME_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"1967 AHSME Problems/Problem 2\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1967_AHSME_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"1967 AHSME Problems/Problem 3\">3</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1967_AHSME_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"1967 AHSME Problems/Problem 4\">4</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1967_AHSME_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"1967 AHSME Problems/Problem 5\">5</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1967_AHSME_Problems/Problem_6\" title=\"1967 AHSME Problems/Problem 6\">6</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1967_AHSME_Problems/Problem_7\" 